WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-Now, you are respected for
your leadership,

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.770
so I thought that we'd have
some fun by asking you,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.673
once and for all, to settle
some of the biggest debates

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.542
of all time.
Does that sound okay?

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.510
-Yeah, I don't think
this is fun. This is serious.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.645
-Yeah. That's right.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.047
Let's do it.
-And I'm prepared.

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.482
-It is time for
"Obama Settles It."

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.784
♪ -Ohh, Obama settles it ♪

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:21.721
♪ Obama settles it ♪

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.556
-Ow! First issue --

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.757
-I like the little lead-in,
by the way.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.393
-Not bad, that was --
-That was pretty good.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.796
I might use that at home.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.064
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.499
The Roots really went for it.
-At dinner.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:35.034
-Yeah. Alright. First issue.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:38.404 line:0%
Does the person flying in the
middle seat get both armrests?

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:41.040 line:0%
-No.
-Yeah.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.311 line:0%
-No. You know,
they have to choose one.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.746 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.848 line:0%
If you're a righty, you --
yeah, you'd have to choose one.

00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:51.450 line:0%
Yeah. You can't get both.
-You got to choose one.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.053 line:0%
You can't have both, no.
-I agree. Good, settled.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:56.423 line:0%
Next -- Oh, I know where
you're going to go with this.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:59.658 line:0%
New York style
or Chicago deep dish?

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:02.662 line:0%
-I'm going to go contrary
to type on this.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.431 line:0%
-What?!
-I love Chicago deep-dish pizza.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.166 line:0%
-Yes!
-I love my hometown.

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:11.070 line:0%
-Yes.
-But New York style,

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:15.175 line:0%
being able to fold it,
walk while you're eating,

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.710 line:0%
there's an efficiency element
to it that,

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.279 line:0%
I think, puts it over the top.

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:21.948 line:0%
No offense, Chicago.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.250 line:0%
I love our pizza.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.919 line:0%
I'm just saying.
-It's settled.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.620 line:0%
-New York's
a little more practical.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.157 line:0%
Chicago deep dish is
basically you have to sit down.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.326 line:0%
You eat it like lasagna, right?
You can't be walking around.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.794 line:0%
-It almost feels the same weight
of your book.

00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:38.530 line:0%
One slice of Chicago deep dish.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.966 line:0%
I do love it as well.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.068 line:0%
Follow-up to this question,
and this is --

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.737 line:0%
I think this is
another no-brainer.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.306 line:0%
-This is a no-- No pineapple.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:52.111 line:0%
I'm from Hawaii and I know you
can't have pineapple on a pizza.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.379 line:0%
-Thank you. Thank you.
This is fantas--

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.214 line:0%
-That's just wrong.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:56.615 line:0%
-It is. Yeah.

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:58.851 line:0%
No. Good. Sorry I even asked.
Alright.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.487 line:0%
-I settled that. Next.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.356 line:0%
-This comes up every December.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:07.227 line:0%
Is "Die Hard" a Christmas movie?

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.961 line:0%
-No.
-Yeah, I agree.

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:11.731 line:0%
-No, "It's A Wonderful Life"
is a Christmas movie.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.999 line:0%
-That's right.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.034 line:0%
-"Charlie Brown Christmas"
is a Christmas movie.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.869 line:0%
"Die Hard" is an action flick

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:19.938 line:0%
that happens to involve,
tangentially, Christmas.

00:02:19.938 --> 00:02:21.174 line:0%
-This is unbelievable.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.975 line:0%
This is the best interview
I've ever done.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:24.444 line:0%
Alright. Next.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:27.280 line:0%
Is it okay to put
ketchup on eggs?

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.216 line:0%
-No.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.052 line:0%
-Next.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:36.622 line:0%
Got it. Should the --
-That's wrong. Next.

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:39.558 line:0%
-Should the toilet roll
hang under or over?

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:40.627 line:0%
-Over.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.994 line:0%
-It's got to be over.
-Yep, I agree.

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:43.796 line:0%
-Tears off easier. Neater.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.832 line:0%
-The other thing is silly.
It's a mistake.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.299 line:0%
Yeah, I agree.
-It's a mistake.

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:50.303 line:0%
-Is a hot dog a sandwich?

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.738 line:0%
-No, a hot dog's a hot dog.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.739 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:55.407 line:0%
-A sandwich is a sandwich.

00:02:55.407 --> 00:02:56.742 line:0%
-Even the way you said that
was perfect.

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.711 line:0%
A hot dog is a hot --
Someone's going to remix that

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.446 line:0%
into, like, a dance jam.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:01.914 line:0%
Hot dog's a hot dog.

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.850 line:0%
Alright.
How do you pronounce the word

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.919 line:0%
at the bottom of my screen?

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.755 line:0%
-Pe-cahn.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.590 line:0%
-Okay. Okay.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.058 line:0%
-Oh, are you disagreeing with me
on this?

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.626 line:0%
You go with the "pee-can" thing?

00:03:14.626 --> 00:03:16.462 line:0%
-Yeah, pee-can.
I mean, I'm not even really --

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.897 line:0%
I'm not --
-Pee-can.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.366 line:0%
-I'm not even a fan of the
pecan, even though that rhymes.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.302 line:0%
But pe-cahn sounds snooty to me.

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:25.371 line:0%
Snooty nut.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.606 line:0%
It's a little snooty?
It's a little elitist?

00:03:27.606 --> 00:03:29.475 line:0%
-It's vas. It's face vas.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.178 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.812 line:0%
-Alright.
-Oh, how about this one?

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:35.647 line:0%
Edge pieces, brownies.

00:03:35.647 --> 00:03:37.850 line:0%
The best or the worst?

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.851 line:0%
-Best.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.219 line:0%
-Yeah, I agree with you, too.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.221 line:0%
-A little crunch.
-Yep.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:45.758 line:0%
-The sort of sugar crystallizes
a little bit.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.893 line:0%
-Yep, I agree.
-It's nice.

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:49.662 line:0%
-I agree. I love it, too.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:50.762 line:0%
Take a look at this.

00:03:50.762 --> 00:03:54.266 line:0%
Is the Mona Lisa smiling?

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:55.368 line:0%
-Slightly.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.603 line:0%
-It's the Mona Lisa smile,
of course.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.639 line:0%
It's a Mona Lisa smile.
It's a type of smile.

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:02.541 line:0%
-She's got secrets.

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:08.280 line:0%
-It's a sly, secretive,
"cat ate the canary" smile.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.749 line:0%
-Uh-huh. I agree.
-That's what's going on.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:12.685 line:0%
-Yep. Next, is cereal a soup?

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.420 line:0%
[ Laughs ]

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.088 line:0%
-[ Laughing ] What?

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.957 line:0%
-I mean, it's like a liquid
in a bowl --

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.993 line:0%
-I mean, some of these
were actual controversies.

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.261 line:0%
This one, no.
What does that mean?

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:23.763 line:0%
-Sorry. I don't know how that
got in there.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.064 line:0%
-Come on. Move on. Next.
-I'm sorry.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.499 line:0%
I don't even know how that
got in there.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.267 line:0%
-That's terrible.
-I agree.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.835 line:0%
Should you tell someone

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:34.173 line:0%
if there's food stuck
in their teeth?

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.042 line:0%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:38.077 line:0%
-Unless it's somebody
you don't like.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.478 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:42.381 line:0%
-And then you might just kind of
let 'em suffer a little bit.

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:46.185 line:0%
It's a small, little bit of --

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.621 line:0%
-It's a small jab.
-You know, little, small --

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.222 line:0%
small bit of shade
that you can throw.

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:53.625 line:0%
-Yeah, I agree.
-Without big moral implications.

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:57.162 line:0%
But if you care about them,
yeah, obviously.

00:04:57.162 --> 00:04:59.465 line:0%
-Yeah.
If you made a sandwich,

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:02.334 line:0%
would you cut the sandwich
diagonally or horizontally?

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.603 line:0%
You have to cut it.

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:06.439 line:0%
-I was about to ask.

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.441 line:0%
I tend not --
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:11.410 line:0%
-I always think, you know,
the people who cut the sandwich,

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.781 line:0%
I admire them because I think,
oh, you know, wow.

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:16.816 line:0%
You -- You --
-Wow. You went the extra step.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.250 line:0%
-That seems like, probably,

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.319 line:0%
what I should do,
and, yet, I never do it.

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:22.454 line:0%
-No, me neither.

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:25.657 line:0%
-But I guess,
if I had to cut it,

00:05:25.657 --> 00:05:28.493 line:0%
maybe I'd go with the diagonal
because there's something about

00:05:28.493 --> 00:05:32.297 line:0%
the point of the --
the pointy edge of the sandwich

00:05:32.297 --> 00:05:34.666 line:0%
that you can put in your mouth
a little bit...

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:35.802 line:0%
-It's an angle.
It's a good bite.

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:37.636 line:0%
-...more efficiently.
There's an angle.

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:40.339 line:0%
-Yeah, it's like the edge of
the brownie.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.241 line:0%
I wish I wrote that one down.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:45.912 line:0%
It's like I'm talking into
a mirror is what it's like.

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:48.247 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.249 line:0%
Finally, last one. One more.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:53.552 line:0%
Is the glass half empty
or half full?

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:55.287 line:0%
-It is always half full.

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:56.488 line:0%
-You heard it here first.

00:05:56.488 --> 00:05:58.524 line:0%
Thank you,
President Barack Obama,

00:05:58.524 --> 00:05:59.692
for settling the biggest

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:02.127
and most important debates
of all time.

00:06:02.127 --> 00:06:04.730
"A Promised Land" is out now,
everybody.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:08.101
We'll be right back with
more "Tonight Show."

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:10.370
Thank you so much!
-Thank you, Jimmy.

